# AWS EC2 Instance & CloudWatch CPU Alarm Setup

This repository contains the setup and documentation for deploying an EC2 instance with an automated CloudWatch CPU utilization alarm and SNS topic notifications using the AWS CLI.

---

## Architecture Overview

1. **EC2 Instance (`xfusion-ec2`)**: An Ubuntu-based virtual machine running in `us-east-1`.
2. **SNS Topic (`xfusion-sns-topic`)**: An existing Amazon SNS topic used to receive alarm notification alerts.
3. **CloudWatch Alarm (`xfusion-alarm`)**: Monitors the CPU utilization of the EC2 instance and triggers an action if threshold limits are exceeded.

---

## Alarm Specifications

| Parameter | Value |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Alarm Name** | `xfusion-alarm` |
| **Metric Name** | `CPUUtilization` |
| **Namespace** | `AWS/EC2` |
| **Statistic** | `Average` |
| **Period** | `300 seconds (5 minutes)` |
| **Evaluation Periods** | `1` |
| **Threshold** | `>= 90%` |
| **Comparison Operator** | `GreaterThanOrEqualToThreshold` |
| **Alarm Action** | `xfusion-sns-topic` |

---

## Deployment Steps

### 1. Set AWS Environment Variables

Ensure your region is set to `us-east-1`:

```bash
export AWS_DEFAULT_REGION="us-east-1"
2. Fetch the Latest Ubuntu 22.04 LTS AMI
Bash
AMI_ID=$(aws ec2 describe-images \
  --owners 099720109477 \
  --filters "Name=name,Values=ubuntu/images/hvm-ssd/ubuntu-jammy-22.04-amd64-server-*" "Name=state,Values=available" \
  --query "reverse(sort_by(Images, &CreationDate))[0].ImageId" \
  --output text)
3. Launch the EC2 Instance
Launch the instance with the required name tag xfusion-ec2:

Bash
INSTANCE_ID=$(aws ec2 run-instances \
  --image-id $AMI_ID \
  --instance-type t2.micro \
  --tag-specifications 'ResourceType=instance,Tags=[{Key=Name,Value=xfusion-ec2}]' \
  --query 'Instances[0].InstanceId' \
  --output text)

echo "Launched Instance ID: $INSTANCE_ID"
4. Retrieve the SNS Topic ARN
Fetch the Amazon Resource Name (ARN) for xfusion-sns-topic:

Bash
TOPIC_ARN=$(aws sns list-topics \
  --query "Topics[?contains(TopicArn, 'xfusion-sns-topic')].TopicArn" \
  --output text)

echo "Target SNS Topic ARN: $TOPIC_ARN"
5. Create the CloudWatch Alarm
Create the alarm targeting the newly created EC2 instance ID:

Bash
aws cloudwatch put-metric-alarm \
  --alarm-name xfusion-alarm \
  --alarm-description "Alarm when CPU exceeds 90% for 5 minutes" \
  --metric-name CPUUtilization \
  --namespace AWS/EC2 \
  --statistic Average \
  --period 300 \
  --evaluation-periods 1 \
  --threshold 90 \
  --comparison-operator GreaterThanOrEqualToThreshold \
  --dimensions Name=InstanceId,Value=$INSTANCE_ID \
  --alarm-actions $TOPIC_ARN
Verification
To verify the setup, run the following AWS CLI commands:

Bash
# Check Instance State
aws ec2 describe-instances --instance-ids $INSTANCE_ID --query "Reservations[*].Instances[*].State.Name" --output text

# Check CloudWatch Alarm Configuration
aws cloudwatch describe-alarms --alarm-names xfusion-alarm
